cff-version: 1.2.0
message: >-
  If you use TackleBox or any of its modules, please cite this repository and
  note which module(s) and version(s) you used (each module's own --version
  flag reports this). See each module's README for module-specific citation
  notes (e.g. FlyForge's CARPDM oligo-pool citation, MetaMerge's
  MEGAN7/metaDMG/Holi citations, Spinner's BLAST/MMseqs2 database notes).
type: software
title: TackleBox
authors:
  - given-names: Tyler
    family-names: Murchie
    email: tyler.murchie@hakai.org
repository-code: "https://github.com/tjmurchie/TackleBox"
license: AGPL-3.0-or-later
keywords:
  - ancient DNA
  - aDNA
  - palaeogenomics
  - hybridization capture
  - bait design
  - reference database curation
  - GBIF
abstract: >-
  TackleBox is a collection of scriptable modules for targeted palaeogenomic
  research developed at the Hakai Institute: FlyForge (bait/probe design),
  FlyGuide (region-specific NCBI reference panel construction from GBIF/
  palaeo-database downloads), MetaMerge (ensemble aDNA classification),
  and Spinner (reference sequence curation and QC).
